WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.400
[Soft music]
Training was completed. Did work change?

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.900
Completion and satisfaction light only the first link of the evidence chain.

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:08.700
Leaders are asking about transfer, performance and the business outcome.

00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:10.800
Evidence Studio. A two-minute evidence check for learning teams. A prototype.

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:16.400
Step 1 of 6. Start from the report you already have.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:23.483
Step 2 of 6. Tick what you actually measured.
The chain lights only where something was observed.

00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:32.200
Step 3 of 6. See how far an honest claim can reach.
Open any link to see what it can’t prove yet.

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.983
Step 4 of 6. Have the numbers? Add them.
The brief says what they can and can’t show.

00:00:39.183 --> 00:00:44.400
Step 5 of 6. Check the workplace.
A “No” marks a barrier to verify before you blame the training.

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:50.600
Step 6 of 6. Leave with a brief your leaders can act on.
Your numbers quoted back, with their limits.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:59.517
All inputs shown are examples. Illustrative, not real data.

00:01:00.067 --> 00:01:02.567
Know what you can claim before someone asks.

00:01:02.567 --> 00:01:06.467
Evidence Studio. Free while it’s a prototype. DennisRGriffin.com
